.idea/
*.sln.iml

# CodeRush
.cr/

# Python Tools for Visual Studio (PTVS)
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Dove/6085 bring-up: copyrighted Xerox firmware ROMs + EEPROM dumps + museum-derived
# reference docs are runtime inputs, not source -- keep them out of the repo.
# ...but OUR OWN work under that tree IS source and must be tracked.  This has now bitten
# twice: TraceRom.cs was destroyed with no git copy to restore from (it was only ever
# force-added), and the harness's operating manual was untracked for a whole session.
# Track our sources/docs by exception so nobody has to remember `git add -f`.
#
# NB the pattern below is deliberate: git will NOT descend into an excluded DIRECTORY, so a
# bare `dove_build_kit/` makes every `!dove_build_kit/...` negation below it silently dead.
# Exclude the CONTENTS (`/*`) and re-include one level at a time instead.
#
# Keep the exceptions to things WE wrote.  Do NOT except the Xerox artifacts -- the boot ROMs,
# the 93C46 U128/U56 dumps, the 8X305 PROMs, the .db microcode, the de-blobbed .mc sources, or
# the museum docs.  eeprom_floppy.bin is deliberately NOT excepted: it is a 3-byte edit of the
# museum U128 dump and still carries that machine's serial, so it IS an EEPROM dump --
# regenerate it with tools/tracerom/make_eeprom_floppy.py rather than committing it.
dove_build_kit/*
!dove_build_kit/tools/
dove_build_kit/tools/*
!dove_build_kit/tools/tracerom/
dove_build_kit/tools/tracerom/*
!dove_build_kit/tools/tracerom/*.cs
!dove_build_kit/tools/tracerom/*.py
!dove_build_kit/tools/tracerom/HANDOFF.md

# Scratch operator-question relay notes from the Dove bring-up sessions.
OPERATOR_QUESTIONS_*.md